#!/usr/bin/env bash
# observer-probe: mesh-mca
#   mesh-observer-effect: a pure READ, safe to run K+3 times. SMCA corrected-error counters; all-zero IS the healthy reading, so drift here is invisible without the control arm
# reflex-cadence: 13,43 * * * *
# mesh-mca — CPU FAULT sense: AMD SMCA per-functional-unit CORRECTED-ERROR counters.
#
# THE AXIS NOBODY WAS READING. This node has sensed thermals (mesh-hw-health), DRAM *bandwidth*,
# the PCIe bus (mesh-pcie-health), NVMe media wear (mesh-nvme-health) and kernel pressure
# (mesh-psi) — and had NO CPU-fault sense at all. Nothing in scripts/ read
# /sys/devices/system/machinecheck; the earlier `grep -l edac` hits that looked like readers were
# the `edac ⊂ redaction` substring collision.
#
# Source: /sys/devices/system/machinecheck/machinecheck<N>/<block>/<sub>/error_count — mode 0444,
# root-owned, WORLD-READABLE. AMD Scalable-MCA threshold blocks. No root, no perf (root-only on
# this node), no RAPL (root-blocked), no debugfs (lockdown=integrity). 117 counters here; the bare
# tree walk is ~20ms and the whole sense (117 x 3 files, parsed + classified) is ~0.9s wall.
#
#   96  per-LOGICAL-CPU  load_store l2_cache insn_fetch floating_point execution_unit decode_unit
#    8  l3_cache_0..7    (CCX-wide, exposed on cpu0)
#    4  umc_{0,1}/{dram_ecc,misc_umc}
#    9  uncore           nbio smu psp mp5 pie coherent_slave_0/1 param_block_0/1
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT THE EDAC DEAD END. capability-dram-bandwidth-sense-amd-uncore-unloaded-…-20260816
# found /sys/devices/system/edac/mc/ empty, confirmed the DIMMs are non-ECC, and correctly said "do
# not file 'load amd64_edac' as a fix — the hardware cannot produce them." That verdict is true for
# exactly 2 of these 117 blocks (umc_0/dram_ecc, umc_1/dram_ecc — the DIMM-ECC path) and FALSE for
# the other 115, which count ON-DIE array ECC/parity that Zen implements whatever DIMMs are fitted.
# A correct finding about one axis had been generalised into blindness about the rest.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT THE AER 0444-THAT-NEVER-INCREMENTS SHAPE (memory: aer-service-binds-on-only-two-
# of-eight-root-ports). show_error_count() in arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/amd.c returns
# MCA_MISC[43:32] - (4095 - threshold_limit) from a live rdmsr_on_cpu. Writing threshold_limit
# reprograms the hardware ErrCnt, so the printed value can only stay 0 if the read really reached
# the MSR: cpu0/l2_cache limit 4095->1000 still printed 0, where a stale/constant read would have
# printed the unsigned underflow 4294964201. Live silicon, measured, then restored. (The kernel
# also instantiates a threshold block only where the hardware reports CntP && !Locked, so the
# directory's existence is itself a hardware assertion.)
#
# Per-block verdict, on the DELTA since the last sample:
#   CLEAN      — 0 lifetime, 0 this interval
#   BASELINE   — no prior sample for this block (or the boot changed — see below)
#   QUIET      — lifetime > 0 but none new this interval. NOT "healed": those errors happened.
#   CORRECTED  — NEW corrected errors this interval. The unit's ECC/parity caught and fixed them;
#                a RISING rate is the earliest honest sign of a degrading core/cache/uncore block.
#   RESET      — the count FELL with no reboot. This is NOT healing (trap 2 below).
#   SATURATED  — count >= threshold_limit: the counter cannot advance, further errors are INVISIBLE.
# Overall = worst (SATURATED > RESET > CORRECTED > QUIET > BASELINE > CLEAN).
#
# ---- THE THREE TRAPS, all of them load-bearing here -------------------------------------
# 1. SMT SIBLINGS HOLD INDEPENDENT MSR STATE — measured both directions (cpu0/cpu8 are
#    thread_siblings_list 0,8; writing one's threshold_limit left the other's error_count alone).
#    So the 96 per-logical-CPU blocks are NOT 48 blocks read twice, and summing them is not an
#    obvious double-count. But whether a REAL corrected error on a physical core increments one
#    thread's counter or both is UNTESTED and honestly unknown — it cannot be settled without ECC
#    RAM or mce-inject. This tool therefore reports per-LOGICAL-CPU blocks and says so; it never
#    prints a per-physical-core figure, because that number would assert the untested half.
# 2. error_count IS NOT MONOTONIC — IT RESETS. At threshold_limit the MCA threshold interrupt
#    fires and threshold_restart_bank() reprograms ErrCnt to 4095-limit, so the count drops to 0.
#    A DROP therefore means ~(limit - prior) MORE errors just passed, never healing
#    (a-wrapping-counters-interval-can-be-undecidable, a-counter-delta-straddles-the-change-
#    instant). It also zeroes on reboot — which is a different claim, so the state file carries
#    boot_id and a boot change re-baselines instead of crying RESET.
#    Residual undecidability, stated not hidden: if a block wrapped a FULL epoch and climbed back
#    to exactly the prior value within one interval, the delta reads 0. At limit=4095 with
#    corrected errors this rare that is not a live concern, but it is the honest bound on the read.
# 3. threshold_limit AND interrupt_enable ARE ROOT-WRITABLE ACTUATORS (0644), not knobs to tune.
#    THIS TOOL NEVER WRITES EITHER — it only reads them, because the reset arithmetic in trap 2
#    depends on the limit and the SATURATED verdict depends on both. A block left at a non-default
#    limit (e.g. by a liveness probe that failed to restore) is REPORTED, since it changes what a
#    reading means.
#
# COVERAGE IS PUBLISHED BESIDE THE VALUE. All-zero is the expected healthy reading, which is
# exactly why a half-broken read's 0 must be distinguishable from this 0: the header carries
# read/discovered blocks and the per-class breakdown, and any shortfall renders BLIND (exit 3),
# never CLEAN. Coverage is also 100% of the INTERVAL, not a sample of it — error_count is an
# accumulator, so the delta spans the whole cadence (a-senses-coverage-is-window-over-cadence).
#
# Exit 2 (honest n/a, never a fake CLEAN): no threshold blocks exposed — Intel, a non-SMCA AMD, a
#   VM, or a kernel without CONFIG_X86_MCE_AMD. mesh-land treats exit 2 as a pass and mesh-autowire
#   SKIPs the reflex, so this stays off every non-AMD-Zen node by the ARTIFACT, not by a vendor name.
# Exit 3 (BLIND — a DIFFERENT claim than exit 2): blocks exist but not all of them could be read.
# Exit 1: a real CPU fault axis moved (CORRECTED / RESET / SATURATED).
#
# Change-gated: rewrites STATE only when a counter moves, but mesh-state-touch's it on EVERY
# successful run so a long-CLEAN node cannot decay to a FALSE-STALE (liveness-touch convention).
#
#   mesh-mca          summary + every non-CLEAN block
#   mesh-mca --raw    every block, including the CLEAN ones
#   mesh-mca --test   synthetic fixtures (both directions of every gate) + a real-hardware read gate
set -uo pipefail

MCA_ROOT="${MESH_MCA_ROOT:-/sys/devices/system/machinecheck}"
STATE="${MESH_MCA_STATE:-$HOME/.mesh/.mca-state}"
BOOTID_FILE="${MESH_MCA_BOOTID:-/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id}"
DEFAULT_LIMIT=4095
RAW=0
[ "${1:-}" = --raw ] && { RAW=1; shift; }

# read a non-negative integer out of a sysfs file; fail (never echo a 0) on missing/unreadable/garbage
read_u32() {
  local f="$1" v
  [ -r "$f" ] || return 1
  v="$(cat "$f" 2>/dev/null)" || return 1
  v="${v%%[[:space:]]*}"
  case "$v" in ''|*[!0-9]*) return 1;; esac
  printf '%s' "$v"
}

# functional class of a threshold block, keyed on the SUB-block name the kernel creates
class_of() {
  case "$1" in
    load_store|l2_cache|insn_fetch|floating_point|execution_unit|decode_unit) echo core ;;
    l3_cache_*) echo l3 ;;
    dram_ecc)   echo umc-ecc ;;
    misc_umc)   echo umc-misc ;;
    *)          echo uncore ;;
  esac
}

# every error_count path the kernel exposes — the DISCOVERED population, independent of readability
discover() {
  local f
  shopt -s nullglob
  for f in "$MCA_ROOT"/machinecheck*/*/*/error_count; do printf '%s\n' "$f"; done
}

# one line per SUCCESSFULLY READ block: "<key> <class> <count> <limit> <interrupt_enable>"
# a block whose error_count cannot be read is OMITTED (the caller sees it as a coverage shortfall),
# never emitted as a fabricated zero.
snapshot() {
  local f rel rest cpu blk sub key cnt lim ie
  while read -r f; do
    [ -n "$f" ] || continue
    cnt="$(read_u32 "$f")" || continue
    rel="${f#"$MCA_ROOT"/}"                  # machinecheck3/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count
    cpu="${rel%%/*}"; cpu="${cpu#machinecheck}"
    rest="${rel#*/}"; blk="${rest%%/*}"
    rest="${rest#*/}"; sub="${rest%%/*}"
    if [ "$blk" = "$sub" ]; then key="cpu$cpu:$sub"; else key="cpu$cpu:$blk/$sub"; fi
    lim="$(read_u32 "${f%/error_count}/threshold_limit")" || lim=-1
    ie="$(read_u32 "${f%/error_count}/interrupt_enable")" || ie=-1
    printf '%s %s %s %s %s\n' "$key" "$(class_of "$sub")" "$cnt" "$lim" "$ie"
  done < <(discover)
}

# <have_prior> <delta> <count> <limit>  ->  verdict
classify() {
  local hp="$1" d="$2" c="$3" lim="$4"
  [ "$lim" -gt 0 ] 2>/dev/null && [ "$c" -ge "$lim" ] && { echo SATURATED; return; }
  [ "$hp" = 0 ] && { echo BASELINE; return; }
  [ "$d" -lt 0 ] && { echo RESET; return; }
  [ "$d" -gt 0 ] && { echo CORRECTED; return; }
  [ "$c" -gt 0 ] && { echo QUIET; return; }
  echo CLEAN
}

rank_of() {
  case "$1" in SATURATED) echo 6;; RESET) echo 5;; CORRECTED) echo 4;; QUIET) echo 3;;
               BASELINE) echo 1;; *) echo 0;; esac
}

# ---- --test: synthetic fixtures (both directions) + a real-hardware read gate --------------
if [ "${1:-}" = --test ]; then
  e=0
  tf="$(mktemp -d)"; trap 'rm -rf "$tf"' EXIT

  # (1) parser: a refusal is a refusal, never a fabricated 0
  printf '7\n' > "$tf/n"; [ "$(read_u32 "$tf/n")" = 7 ] || { echo "test: read_u32 number FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf 'nope\n' > "$tf/g"; read_u32 "$tf/g" >/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "test: read_u32 must reject garbage FAIL"; e=1; }
  : > "$tf/em";  read_u32 "$tf/em" >/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "test: read_u32 must reject empty FAIL"; e=1; }
  read_u32 "$tf/nothere" >/dev/null 2>&1 && { echo "test: read_u32 must reject missing FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (2) class_of truth table — incl. the two DIMM-ECC blocks that must NOT be lumped with the rest
  for pair in load_store:core l2_cache:core insn_fetch:core floating_point:core execution_unit:core \
              decode_unit:core l3_cache_0:l3 l3_cache_7:l3 dram_ecc:umc-ecc misc_umc:umc-misc \
              nbio:uncore smu:uncore psp:uncore mp5:uncore pie:uncore coherent_slave_0:uncore \
              param_block_1:uncore; do
    [ "$(class_of "${pair%%:*}")" = "${pair##*:}" ] || { echo "test: class_of ${pair%%:*} FAIL"; e=1; }
  done

  # (3) classifier truth table — every verdict, including the two that must never read as healing
  [ "$(classify 0 0 0 4095)"    = BASELINE ]  || { echo "test: cls BASELINE FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 1 0 0 4095)"    = CLEAN ]     || { echo "test: cls CLEAN FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 1 0 12 4095)"   = QUIET ]     || { echo "test: cls QUIET FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 1 3 12 4095)"   = CORRECTED ] || { echo "test: cls CORRECTED FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 1 -500 0 4095)" = RESET ]     || { echo "test: cls RESET FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 1 0 4095 4095)" = SATURATED ] || { echo "test: cls SATURATED FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(classify 0 0 4095 4095)" = SATURATED ] || { echo "test: cls SATURATED must beat BASELINE FAIL"; e=1; }

  # ---- a synthetic /sys tree we control end to end ----------------------------------------
  # mkblk <cpuN> <block> <sub> <count> [limit] [ie]
  mkblk() {
    local p="$tf/sys/machinecheck$1/$2/$3"; mkdir -p "$p"
    printf '%s\n' "$4" > "$p/error_count"
    printf '%s\n' "${5:-4095}" > "$p/threshold_limit"
    printf '%s\n' "${6:-1}" > "$p/interrupt_enable"
  }
  bid="$tf/bootid"; printf 'boot-AAAA\n' > "$bid"
  run() { env MESH_MCA_ROOT="$tf/sys" MESH_MCA_STATE="$tf/st" MESH_MCA_BOOTID="$bid" bash "$0" "$@" 2>&1; }

  rm -rf "$tf/sys"; rm -f "$tf/st"
  mkblk 0 l2_cache l2_cache 0; mkblk 0 umc_0 dram_ecc 0; mkblk 8 l2_cache l2_cache 0

  # (4) snapshot skips a directory with no error_count, never inventing a zero for it
  mkdir -p "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/power"                     # sysfs puts non-block dirs here too
  mkdir -p "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/decode_unit/decode_unit"   # block dir, NO error_count
  n="$(env MESH_MCA_ROOT="$tf/sys" bash -c 'MCA_ROOT="$MESH_MCA_ROOT"; '"$(declare -f read_u32 class_of discover snapshot)"'; snapshot' | grep -c .)"
  [ "$n" = 3 ] || { echo "test: snapshot must emit exactly the 3 readable blocks (got $n) FAIL"; e=1; }
  rmdir "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/decode_unit/decode_unit" "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/decode_unit"

  # (5) first sample baselines and does NOT claim health it has no interval for
  o1="$(run)"; rc1=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$o1" | grep -q '^mca: BASELINE' || { echo "test: first sample must render BASELINE — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$o1"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rc1" = 0 ] || { echo "test: BASELINE must exit 0 (got $rc1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$o1" | grep -q 'coverage 3/3 blocks' || { echo "test: header must publish coverage — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$o1"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  o2="$(run)"; rc2=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$o2" | grep -q '^mca: CLEAN' || { echo "test: settled all-zero sample must be CLEAN — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$o2"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rc2" = 0 ] || { echo "test: CLEAN must exit 0 (got $rc2) FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (6) COVERAGE GATE, RED-first: the SAME all-zero tree that just read CLEAN must flip to BLIND
  #     the moment one counter cannot be read. This is the whole point of publishing coverage —
  #     a half-broken read's 0 must not be this 0. (chmod 000 denies the owner too, we are uid!=0.)
  chmod 000 "$tf/sys/machinecheck8/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  ob="$(run)"; rcb=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$ob" | grep -q '^mca: BLIND' || { echo "test: an unreadable counter must render BLIND, not CLEAN — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$ob"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$ob" | grep -q 'coverage 2/3 blocks' || { echo "test: BLIND must publish the SHORTFALL — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$ob"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcb" = 3 ] || { echo "test: BLIND must exit 3, distinct from n/a's 2 (got $rcb) FAIL"; e=1; }
  chmod 644 "$tf/sys/machinecheck8/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"

  # (7) CORRECTED fires on a real rise
  printf '3\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  oc="$(run)"; rcc=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$oc" | grep -q '^mca: CORRECTED' || { echo "test: a rise must render CORRECTED — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$oc"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$oc" | grep -q 'cpu0:l2_cache .*CORRECTED.*+3' || { echo "test: CORRECTED must name the block and the delta FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcc" = 1 ] || { echo "test: CORRECTED must exit 1 (got $rcc) FAIL"; e=1; }
  # and it decays to QUIET, never to CLEAN — those 3 errors still happened this boot
  oq="$(run)"
  printf '%s\n' "$oq" | grep -q '^mca: QUIET' || { echo "test: lifetime>0 with no new errors must be QUIET, never CLEAN — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$oq"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (8) RESET IS NOT HEALING — both directions of the same drop, the trap-2 gate.
  #     (a) SAME boot: count falls 3->0 => RESET, exit 1, and it must SAY errors passed.
  printf '0\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  or="$(run)"; rcr=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$or" | grep -q '^mca: RESET' || { echo "test: a drop with no reboot must render RESET — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$or"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$or" | grep -qi 'not healing' || { echo "test: RESET must state it is NOT healing FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$or" | grep -q 'at least 4092' || { echo "test: RESET must quantify the errors that passed (limit-prior = 4095-3) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcr" = 1 ] || { echo "test: RESET must exit 1 (got $rcr) FAIL"; e=1; }
  #     (b) SAME drop across a BOOT CHANGE: must re-baseline and claim NOTHING about errors.
  rm -f "$tf/st"; printf '3\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  run >/dev/null; run >/dev/null                                  # settle a prior at 3 under boot-AAAA
  printf 'boot-BBBB\n' > "$bid"
  printf '0\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  ob2="$(run)"; rcb2=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$ob2" | grep -q '^mca: BASELINE' || { echo "test: the same drop across a REBOOT must re-baseline, not cry RESET — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$ob2"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$ob2" | grep -q 'RESET' && { echo "test: a reboot must not be reported as RESET FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcb2" = 0 ] || { echo "test: a reboot re-baseline must exit 0 (got $rcb2) FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (9) SATURATED — a counter pinned at its limit cannot advance, so its ZERO DELTA is blindness,
  #     not quiet. Red-first: at limit-1 with the same delta it must NOT fire.
  rm -f "$tf/st"; printf 'boot-AAAA\n' > "$bid"
  printf '4094\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  run >/dev/null; os0="$(run)"
  printf '%s\n' "$os0" | grep -q 'SATURATED' && { echo "test: limit-1 must NOT read as SATURATED FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '4095\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  os="$(run)"; rcs=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$os" | grep -q '^mca: SATURATED' || { echo "test: count at threshold_limit must render SATURATED — got: $(printf '%s\n' "$os"|head -1) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcs" = 1 ] || { echo "test: SATURATED must exit 1 (got $rcs) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '0\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"

  # (10) ACTUATOR GATE (trap 3): the tool must NEVER write threshold_limit / interrupt_enable.
  #      Asserted on the ARTIFACT — content AND mtime of every writable actuator file in the
  #      fixture, across a full run — not on the source text.
  rm -f "$tf/st"
  printf '1000\n' > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/umc_0/dram_ecc/threshold_limit"   # a non-default limit
  printf '0\n'    > "$tf/sys/machinecheck0/umc_0/dram_ecc/interrupt_enable"  # and a disarmed block
  before="$(find "$tf/sys" \( -name threshold_limit -o -name interrupt_enable \) -printf '%p %s %T@ ' -exec cat {} \; | sort)"
  oa="$(run --raw)"
  after="$(find "$tf/sys" \( -name threshold_limit -o -name interrupt_enable \) -printf '%p %s %T@ ' -exec cat {} \; | sort)"
  [ "$before" = "$after" ] || { echo "test: the sense WROTE an actuator (threshold_limit/interrupt_enable changed) FAIL"; e=1; }
  #      ...and a block left off-default must be REPORTED, since it changes what a reading means
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -q 'arming:' || { echo "test: must publish an arming line FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -q 'cpu0:umc_0/dram_ecc' || { echo "test: an off-default block must be NAMED in the arming line FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -q 'limit=1000' || { echo "test: the arming line must carry the non-default limit FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -q 'irq=off' || { echo "test: the arming line must carry the disarmed interrupt FAIL"; e=1; }
  #      --raw prints every block; the default view prints only the non-CLEAN ones
  [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -c '^  cpu')" -ge 3 ] || { echo "test: --raw must list every block FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (11) THE DIMM-ECC CAVEAT must travel with the reading: 2 of 117 are the DRAM-ECC path and are
  #      structurally silent on non-ECC modules, so their 0 is not an observation.
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -q 'umc-ecc' || { echo "test: coverage must break out the umc-ecc class FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$oa" | grep -qi 'structural, not observed' || { echo "test: the dram_ecc 0 must be labelled structural FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (12) n/a is a CLAIM about the node, never a green — and it must not write state
  mkdir -p "$tf/empty"
  on="$(env MESH_MCA_ROOT="$tf/empty" MESH_MCA_STATE="$tf/st-na" MESH_MCA_BOOTID="$bid" bash "$0" 2>&1)"; rcn=$?
  printf '%s\n' "$on" | grep -q '^mca: n/a' || { echo "test: an empty tree must render n/a — got: $on FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$rcn" = 2 ] || { echo "test: n/a must exit 2 so autowire SKIPs off AMD Zen (got $rcn) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ -e "$tf/st-na" ] && { echo "test: an n/a run must not write state FAIL"; e=1; }

  # (13) CHANGE-GATE and LIVENESS-TOUCH are two INDEPENDENT halves and each needs its own gate
  #      (memory: liveness-touch-content-axis-goes-unchecked). mtime alone cannot separate them —
  #      a rewrite moves mtime exactly like a touch does, which is precisely how the broken
  #      $(cat)-strips-the-newline compare hid here until a mutant exposed it.
  #      DISCRIMINATOR: a mode-0444 state file REFUSES a rewrite (EACCES on stderr) while still
  #      accepting an mtime touch from its owner (verified on this node).
  rm -rf "$tf/sys2"; st2="$tf/st2"
  mkdir -p "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache"
  printf '0\n' > "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  printf '4095\n' > "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/threshold_limit"
  printf '1\n' > "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/interrupt_enable"
  run2() { env MESH_MCA_ROOT="$tf/sys2" MESH_MCA_STATE="$st2" MESH_MCA_BOOTID="$bid" bash "$0" "$@"; }
  rm -f "$st2"; run2 >/dev/null 2>&1                      # seed the state at the settled value
  seeded="$(cat "$st2")"
  #      (a) VALUE UNCHANGED -> the content write must NOT happen, but mtime MUST still move
  chmod 444 "$st2"; touch -d '1 hour ago' "$st2"; old_m="$(stat -c %Y "$st2")"
  err_a="$(run2 2>&1 >/dev/null)"
  case "$err_a" in *[Pp]ermission*|*cannot*) echo "test: change-gate REWROTE an unchanged state (it must only write when a counter moves): $err_a FAIL"; e=1 ;; esac
  [ "$(stat -c %Y "$st2")" -gt "$old_m" ] || { echo "test: an unchanged value must still TOUCH the state (mtime=liveness, else a value-frozen live sense reads as STALE) FAIL"; e=1; }
  [ "$(cat "$st2")" = "$seeded" ] || { echo "test: the touch must be content-preserving FAIL"; e=1; }
  chmod 644 "$st2"
  #      (b) VALUE CHANGED -> the content write MUST happen (a gate stuck shut is as bad as one stuck open)
  printf '9\n' > "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"
  run2 >/dev/null 2>&1
  grep -q 'cpu0:l2_cache 9 ' "$st2" || { echo "test: a MOVED counter must be written through to the state (got: $(cat "$st2")) FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '0\n' > "$tf/sys2/machinecheck0/l2_cache/l2_cache/error_count"

  # (14) REAL-HARDWARE READ GATE — a parser that only ever meets its own fixtures asserts nothing
  #      about /sys. A live read must produce well-formed counters at FULL coverage, or exit 2.
  ndisc="$(discover | grep -c .)"
  if [ "$ndisc" = 0 ]; then
    echo "test: no SMCA threshold block on this node — honest n/a (exit 2)"
    [ "$e" = 0 ] && exit 2 || exit 1
  fi
  real="$(snapshot)"
  nread="$(printf '%s\n' "$real" | grep -c .)"
  [ "$nread" = "$ndisc" ] || { echo "test: live read covered $nread of $ndisc discovered blocks FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$real" | awk 'NF!=5 || $3 ~ /[^0-9]/ || $4 ~ /[^-0-9]/ || $5 ~ /[^-0-9]/ {bad=1} END{exit bad}' \
    || { echo "test: live read produced a malformed/non-numeric block line FAIL"; e=1; }
  printf '%s\n' "$real" | awk '$2 !~ /^(core|l3|umc-ecc|umc-misc|uncore)$/ {bad=1} END{exit bad}' \
    || { echo "test: live read produced an unclassified block FAIL"; e=1; }
  # the actuators on the REAL tree must be untouched by a real run too (trap 3, live path)
  lbefore="$(find "$MCA_ROOT" \( -name threshold_limit -o -name interrupt_enable \) -exec cat {} \; | md5sum)"
  env MESH_MCA_STATE="$tf/st-live" bash "$0" >/dev/null 2>&1
  lafter="$(find "$MCA_ROOT" \( -name threshold_limit -o -name interrupt_enable \) -exec cat {} \; | md5sum)"
  [ "$lbefore" = "$lafter" ] || { echo "test: a LIVE run changed a real threshold_limit/interrupt_enable FAIL"; e=1; }

  [ "$e" = 0 ] && echo "test: PASS (real read: $nread/$ndisc SMCA threshold blocks)" || echo "test: FAIL"
  exit "$e"
fi

# ---- live run -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
discovered="$(discover | grep -c .)"
if [ "$discovered" = 0 ]; then
  echo "mca: n/a — no AMD SMCA threshold blocks under $MCA_ROOT (Intel, a non-SMCA AMD, a VM, or no CONFIG_X86_MCE_AMD). Not a clean CPU: an unreadable axis."
  exit 2
fi

cur="$(snapshot)"
nread="$(printf '%s\n' "$cur" | grep -c .)"

# per-class coverage, so a shortfall is attributable and the umc-ecc caveat can be stated
declare -A CLS_N
while read -r _k cls _c _l _i; do
  [ -n "${cls:-}" ] || continue
  CLS_N["$cls"]=$(( ${CLS_N["$cls"]:-0} + 1 ))
done <<< "$cur"
cov_break=""
for cls in core l3 umc-ecc umc-misc uncore; do
  [ -n "${CLS_N[$cls]+x}" ] && cov_break+="${cov_break:+ · }${CLS_N[$cls]} $cls"
done

# COVERAGE GATE — all-zero is the expected healthy reading, which is exactly why a partial read
# must never wear it. A shortfall is a claim about the SENSE, distinct from n/a (no hardware).
if [ "$nread" -lt "$discovered" ]; then
  echo "mca: BLIND — coverage $nread/$discovered blocks (${cov_break:-none readable}); $((discovered-nread)) SMCA counter(s) present but unreadable, so an all-zero reading would be the sense's 0, not the CPU's. Not CLEAN."
  exit 3
fi

boot_now="$(cat "$BOOTID_FILE" 2>/dev/null)"; boot_now="${boot_now:-unknown}"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$STATE")" 2>/dev/null

boot_prev=""; have_state=0
declare -A P_CNT P_LIM
if [ -s "$STATE" ]; then
  have_state=1
  while read -r k a b _rest; do
    case "$k" in ''|'#'*) [ "$k" = '#boot' ] && boot_prev="$a"; continue;; esac
    P_CNT["$k"]=$a; P_LIM["$k"]=$b
  done < "$STATE"
fi
# A boot change zeroes every counter: the prior sample is not comparable, so re-baseline rather
# than report 117 phantom RESETs. This is a DIFFERENT claim from a same-boot drop (trap 2).
boot_changed=0
[ "$have_state" = 1 ] && [ "$boot_prev" != "$boot_now" ] && boot_changed=1

worst=CLEAN; worst_rank=0; report=""; new_state="#boot $boot_now"$'\n'
off_default=""; n_irq_off=0; n_lim_off=0
while read -r key cls cnt lim ie; do
  [ -n "$key" ] || continue
  hp=1
  { [ "$have_state" = 0 ] || [ "$boot_changed" = 1 ] || [ -z "${P_CNT[$key]+x}" ]; } && hp=0
  prev=${P_CNT[$key]:-0}; plim=${P_LIM[$key]:--1}
  d=$(( cnt - prev ))
  v="$(classify "$hp" "$d" "$cnt" "$lim")"
  r="$(rank_of "$v")"; [ "$r" -gt "$worst_rank" ] && { worst_rank=$r; worst=$v; }

  note=""
  case "$v" in
    CORRECTED) note=" (+$d this interval, lifetime $cnt)" ;;
    QUIET)     note=" (lifetime $cnt this boot — those errors happened; QUIET is not healed)" ;;
    RESET)     # the count fell with no reboot: the threshold interrupt fired and reprogrammed ErrCnt
               local_lim=$plim; [ "$local_lim" -le 0 ] 2>/dev/null && local_lim=$lim
               passed="unknown"
               [ "$local_lim" -gt 0 ] 2>/dev/null && passed=$(( local_lim - prev ))
               note=" ($prev -> $cnt with no reboot: the MCA threshold interrupt fired, so at least $passed more corrected errors passed — this is NOT healing)" ;;
    SATURATED) note=" (count $cnt >= threshold_limit $lim: the counter cannot advance, further corrected errors on this block are INVISIBLE)" ;;
    BASELINE)  note=" (lifetime $cnt; no comparable prior sample — rate not yet knowable)" ;;
  esac
  # CLEAN is the whole node's expected reading and BASELINE fires on all N blocks at once after
  # every boot; both are header-level facts, so the default view lists only the blocks that moved.
  case "$v" in CLEAN|BASELINE) [ "$RAW" = 1 ] && report+="  $key [$cls] $v$note"$'\n' ;;
               *)              report+="  $key [$cls] $v$note"$'\n' ;; esac

  [ "$ie" = 0 ] && { n_irq_off=$((n_irq_off+1)); off_default+="${off_default:+, }$key irq=off"; }
  if [ "$lim" != "$DEFAULT_LIMIT" ]; then
    n_lim_off=$((n_lim_off+1))
    [ "$lim" = -1 ] && off_default+="${off_default:+, }$key limit=unreadable" \
                    || off_default+="${off_default:+, }$key limit=$lim"
  fi
  new_state+="$key $cnt $lim $ie"$'\n'
done <<< "$cur"

boot_note=""
[ "$boot_changed" = 1 ] && boot_note=" · boot changed since the last sample, counters zeroed — re-baselined, no error claim made"
echo "mca: $worst — coverage $nread/$discovered blocks ($cov_break)$boot_note"
printf '%s' "$report"

# Coverage is not only how MANY blocks, but what a 0 from each one is EVIDENCE of.
[ -n "${CLS_N[umc-ecc]+x}" ] && echo "  note: the ${CLS_N[umc-ecc]} umc-ecc block(s) are the DIMM-ECC path — on non-ECC modules they cannot count, so their 0 is structural, not observed. The other $(( nread - ${CLS_N[umc-ecc]} )) count on-die array ECC/parity and read regardless of DIMM ECC."
[ -n "${CLS_N[core]+x}" ] && echo "  note: the ${CLS_N[core]} core block(s) are per-LOGICAL-CPU with independent MSR state (measured); whether a real corrected error increments one SMT thread's counter or both is UNTESTED, so no per-physical-core figure is derived here."

# Arming: read-only. These are root-writable ACTUATORS and this tool never writes them — but a
# block left off-default changes what its reading means, so it is reported.
if [ -z "$off_default" ]; then
  echo "  arming: threshold_limit=$DEFAULT_LIMIT and interrupt_enable=on across all $nread blocks (read-only sense — never written here)"
else
  echo "  arming: $n_lim_off block(s) off the default threshold_limit=$DEFAULT_LIMIT, $n_irq_off with the threshold interrupt disarmed — $off_default (read-only sense — never written here; restore them at the source)"
fi

# Change-gated write. The comparison is BYTE-EXACT via cmp, deliberately not
# [ "$new_state" != "$(cat "$STATE")" ]: command substitution strips trailing newlines from ONE
# side only, so that form never compares equal and the "change gate" writes on every single run —
# which also makes the liveness-touch below untestable, since the write moves mtime by itself
# (two-renderings-of-a-value-must-be-canonicalized; caught by the test-13 mutant, 2026-08-18).
if ! printf '%s' "$new_state" | cmp -s - "$STATE" 2>/dev/null; then
  printf '%s' "$new_state" > "$STATE"
fi
# ran-live (mtime) is a DIFFERENT fact from value-changed (content): an all-CLEAN node holds the
# same 117 zeros for weeks, and without this touch the mtime-aging watchdogs read it as a dead reflex.
mesh-state-touch "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || touch "$STATE" 2>/dev/null

case "$worst" in SATURATED|RESET|CORRECTED) exit 1;; *) exit 0;; esac
